# Manual API tests for the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
# Start RestaurantApplication first, then run the requests from top to bottom
# (click the green arrow next to each request). Ids assume a freshly started application.

### 1. Add a table
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tables
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": 5, "seats": 4 }

### 2. Add menu items
POST http://localhost:8080/api/menu
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Tripe Soup", "category": "APPETIZER", "price": 22.50, "available": true }

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/menu
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Papanasi", "category": "DESSERT", "price": 25.00, "available": true }

### 3. The whole menu / filtered by category
GET http://localhost:8080/api/menu

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/menu?category=DESSERT

### 4. Update a menu item
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/menu/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Tripe Soup", "category": "APPETIZER", "price": 24.00, "available": true }

### 5. Reservation -> 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Andrei Popescu", "phone": "0722123456", "tableId": 1, "dateTime": "2030-12-20T19:00:00", "partySize": 4 }

### 6. Overlapping reservation on the same table -> 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Maria Ionescu", "phone": "0733111222", "tableId": 1, "dateTime": "2030-12-20T20:00:00", "partySize": 2 }

### 7. Order: 2 x Tripe Soup + 1 x Papanasi -> 201, total computed by the server
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tableId": 1, "items": [ { "menuItemId": 1, "quantity": 2 }, { "menuItemId": 2, "quantity": 1 } ] }

### 8. Order lifecycle: NEW -> IN_PREPARATION
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "IN_PREPARATION" }

### 9. Forbidden transition (back to NEW) -> 409
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "NEW" }

### 10. Orders by status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders?status=IN_PREPARATION

### 11. Invalid data -> 400 with one message per field
POST http://localhost:8080/api/menu
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "price": -1 }
